{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Systems","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","externalID":"Systems"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"system","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Declare a System","anchor":"Declare-a-System","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for you: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also conform a type to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by hand and write its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives the whole world. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for when to do that."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" require one system to run after or before another; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"kind":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","title":"SystemParameter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemParameter","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"type":"text","text":"’s closure."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleBuilder"}],"title":"ScheduleBuilder"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"title":"CyclicOrdering","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"title":"ScheduledSystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","title":"ResourceReader","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"title":"SystemTiming","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","title":"EventReader","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","title":"System()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Query"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","role":"collection"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","title":"access","required":true,"role":"symbol","defaultImplementations":1,"abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Access","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ForwardChanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"title":"UpdateEvents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has had its chance to read them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"title":"Update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"title":"Ambiguity","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Ambiguity"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardEvents"}],"title":"ForwardEvents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardEvents"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule can await the events.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SystemSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemSet","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"title":"MainActorSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SystemProfile","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"kind":"article","title":"Declaring Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"title":"ambiguities()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"title":"ResourceWriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","title":"Driving a World from an App","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it read results and take part in a step.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"title":"RemovedComponents","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RemovedComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"title":"System","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","required":true,"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"run(in:)"}}}